{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"7c93a00f0b1d3f79","name":"card_unit_38th_independent","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_38th_independent","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"38th INDEPENDENT","text":"Cannot attack or move. Suppress it if you have 4+ copies. Duplicate this unit when you lose a kredit slot.","flavorText":"The 38th Independent Mixed Brigade was an infantry brigade of the Imperial Japanese Army, formed in June 1944 from the 17th Division. It was attached to the 17th Army and placed under Major General Kesao Kijima. The brigade entered the Bougainville campaign at a time when Japanese forces were already under heavy pressure. Allied control of the air and seas made supply difficult, while Japanese units on the island were increasingly cut off from one another. The brigade is best known for its role in the Battle of Pearl Ridge. There, it opposed the Australian advance across steep and difficult jungle terrain. The fighting lasted three days and ended on 1 January 1945, when the brigade was defeated. After the battle, its intended retreat south toward Buin was refused. This left the formation isolated around Numa Numa on Bougainville Island’s east coast. It remained there until the end of hostilities, separated from the main Japanese concentration in the south.","faction":"Japan","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":3,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_38th_independent","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_38th_independent_title","SourceString":"38th INDEPENDENT","LocalizedString":"38th INDEPENDENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"6F10BBE340A80BB0BD9567854A6AFA9B","SourceString":"Cannot attack or move. Suppress it if you have 4+ copies. Duplicate this unit when you lose a kredit slot.","LocalizedString":"Cannot attack or move. Suppress it if you have 4+ copies. Duplicate this unit when you lose a kredit slot."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_38th_independent_history","SourceString":"The 38th Independent Mixed Brigade was an infantry brigade of the Imperial Japanese Army, formed in June 1944 from the 17th Division. It was attached to the 17th Army and placed under Major General Kesao Kijima. The brigade entered the Bougainville campaign at a time when Japanese forces were already under heavy pressure. Allied control of the air and seas made supply difficult, while Japanese units on the island were increasingly cut off from one another. The brigade is best known for its role in the Battle of Pearl Ridge. There, it opposed the Australian advance across steep and difficult jungle terrain. The fighting lasted three days and ended on 1 January 1945, when the brigade was defeated. After the battle, its intended retreat south toward Buin was refused. This left the formation isolated around Numa Numa on Bougainville Island’s east coast. It remained there until the end of hostilities, separated from the main Japanese concentration in the south.","LocalizedString":"The 38th Independent Mixed Brigade was an infantry brigade of the Imperial Japanese Army, formed in June 1944 from the 17th Division. It was attached to the 17th Army and placed under Major General Kesao Kijima. The brigade entered the Bougainville campaign at a time when Japanese forces were already under heavy pressure. Allied control of the air and seas made supply difficult, while Japanese units on the island were increasingly cut off from one another. The brigade is best known for its role in the Battle of Pearl Ridge. There, it opposed the Australian advance across steep and difficult jungle terrain. The fighting lasted three days and ended on 1 January 1945, when the brigade was defeated. After the battle, its intended retreat south toward Buin was refused. This left the formation isolated around Numa Numa on Bougainville Island’s east coast. It remained there until the end of hostilities, separated from the main Japanese concentration in the south."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","receivedAbilitiesFromCards":[{"Key":"cantMove","Value":{"CardsGivingAbility":[0]}},{"Key":"cantAttack","Value":{"CardsGivingAbility":[0]}}],"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/38th_INDEPENDENT.38th_INDEPENDENT","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":349.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_38th_independent_photo","SourceString":"Surrendered Japanese soldiers, Bougainville, 1945.","LocalizedString":"Surrendered Japanese soldiers, Bougainville, 1945."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryM'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryM.46"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeMedium_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeMedium.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_AttackInfantry_C","SubPathString":""},"Notes":"Image from Y.Takani not licensed yet","isHQDamage":true},"variables":[{"name":"count","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"unitsToSuppress","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_unit_38th_independent","owner":"card_unit_38th_independent_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variabl